1. Scope and status

	•	Purpose and PoC status, with GCP still the production platform.
	•	In scope: cessda-mgmt, cessda-svc and CVS staging.
	•	Out of scope: other products, production cutover.

2. Architecture (one diagram plus a few lines)

	•	cessda-mgmt: Jenkins, ArgoCD, Prometheus, Grafana and Alertmanager.
	•	cessda-svc: CVS workloads, Elasticsearch, MySQL and the registry.
	•	Platform stack: Talos Linux, Cilium Gateway API, cert-manager (Let's Encrypt), and the Cinder storage class.

3. Build and deployment flow

	•	The cluster build runs through a Jenkins pipeline, with the cluster config in the cessda-mgmt-gitops repo and ArgoCD syncing it.
	•	CVS flow: push to main in cessda.cvs.two → Jenkins builds a Docker-in-Docker image → push to GHCR with an immutable tag (main-<build>) → auto-trigger deployment_using_helm_charts → Helm deploys to Safespring.
	•	Elasticsearch uses a custom image with the ICU plugin.

4. CVS components

	•	Done: frontend, Elasticsearch (ECK) and MySQL.
	•	Pending: the contentguide, userguide, mailrelay and reverse components, plus the HTTPRoute fan-out.

5. Security and secrets

	•	SOPS/age with KSOPS for secrets in Git.
	•	Registry credentials, and the baseline versus privileged PodSecurity setting for the Jenkins namespace.
	•	IP restrictions at the Safespring security-group layer.

6. Monitoring and operations

	•	Alerting rules for certificate expiry, Elasticsearch health and PVC capacity.
	•	Certificate renewal, and the backup plan for MySQL and Elasticsearch.
	•	Rollback: RollingUpdate keeps the old ReplicaSet running if a deploy fails.

7. Risks and known gaps

	•	MySQL is single-instance, not HA, and Elasticsearch runs one node.
	•	No LoadBalancer on Safespring, so NodePort and Gateway are used instead.
	•	The Jenkins parameter default latest is never pushed, so manual deploys can fail.
	•	Certificate renewals for the management hostnames are still being investigated.
	•	The mgmt cluster build depends on Jenkins, and that Jenkins runs on cessda-mgmt itself.

8. Plan and next steps

	•	Finish the pending CVS components and move MySQL under Helm.
	•	Resize Elasticsearch storage and address the HA gaps.
	•	Run a full staging test of the pipeline, then agree success criteria for moving CVS off GCP.

